00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:03.060
New models indicate that planets in warm Jupiter systems can scatter one another during formation.

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:08.680
Simulations show how initial disk conditions shape the final orbital architectures.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:14.120
Scattering events can eject smaller bodies or move orbits into resonant configurations.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:20.700
The work focuses on systems where giant planets orbit closer to their stars than Jupiter does to the sun.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.300
The models incorporate both gas-disc interactions and gravitational encounters between

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:33.480
planets. The scattering process alters orbital architectures over time. The Expedition 75 crew

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:38.360
completed lead-free soldering experiments and virtual reality lunar landing simulations.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.720
The team also prepared for an upcoming cargo vehicle arrival while maintaining housekeeping

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:49.920
and exercise routines. The soldering tests evaluated techniques for future spacecraft repairs

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:55.800
in microgravity. Lunar simulations used virtual reality tools to rehearse landing procedures.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:06:01.960
Cargo preparations include inventory checks and birthing mechanism tests ahead of the vehicle's arrival.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.620
Housekeeping and exercise routines continued alongside the research activities.

