Astronomers report that the window for observing a giant planet's unusual orbit is closing rapidly.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:19.780
The planet's path shows signs of past dynamical interactions that altered its inclination and eccentricity.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:24.960
Telescope schedules are being adjusted to capture the remaining favorable viewing geometry.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:30.580
symmetry. Follow-up observations are needed before the geometry changes. Without new data,

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:36.660
the system's formation history may remain poorly constrained. NASA's Nancy Grace Roman space

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:42.300
telescope captured its first starlight during testing. Light from a single star passed through

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:48.120
the full optical chain and reached the detectors. Engineers are using the data to verify focus

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:53.760
and throughput across the wide field instrument. The milestone confirms the telescope's optical

00:06:53.760 --> 00:07:00.020
system is functioning as designed. Further calibration steps remain before science operations begin.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.440
The telescope is scheduled for additional alignment checks in the coming months.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:10.080
Mars express images show purple regions on the surface under specific lighting and mineral

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:15.840
